    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics isn't something I deeply care about, but I do understand the basics. I got through lower secondary school with a decent grasp of algebra and geometry, mostly through repetition and memorization. I don't find it interesting, but it's useful for everyday life. I enjoy more creative things like art and cycling, which I think are more satisfying.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I rarely get anxious about math. It's not something that stresses me out. If I'm stuck on a problem, I usually just take a break and come back to it later. I'm not afraid of getting a wrong answer. I think it's more about being patient. I enjoy solving problems, even if it takes time.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a simple AI app to help me understand fractions and equations. It explained things in a simple way, and I found it really helpful. It didn't replace my understanding, but it helped me see the process more clearly. I used it mostly for self-study, and I found it convenient.",
