    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "You first take the derivative of the function, f'(x). Then you set f'(x) equal to zero and solve for x. Those x values are the x-coordinates of the stationary points. Plug those x-values back into the original function to find the y-coordinates. These give you the points where the curve stops increasing or decreasing.",
